WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.192
The school outline names normal delivery and several complications. We will follow the clinical sequence from recognizing impending birth through separate maternal and newborn reassessment.
学校周纲点名正常分娩及多种并发。这里按临床顺序，从识别即将出生一直到母婴独立复评。

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:24.432
The narrative foundation is the reviewed birth and postpartum sections of the supplied Nancy textbook. Current local procedures qualify older instructions rather than being silently mixed with them.
正文基础是已审读的自备Nancy分娩及产后章节。旧指令需以现行当地程序限定，不能悄悄混在一起。

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:33.336
This is preparation for supervised practical learning, not an added school online module or a claim that reading certifies delivery maneuvers.
这是监督实操学习准备，不是新增学校线上模块，也不声称阅读即可认证助产手法。

00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:44.568
The newborn resuscitation algorithm is a separate next session. Here, always prepare for it while maintaining maternal care and recognizing when birth has become complicated.
新生儿复苏算法是下一独立节。这里要始终为其准备，同时维持母体照护并识别分娩何时变复杂。

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:53.832
The first stage ends when the cervix is fully dilated. Effacement describes thinning and shortening, while dilation describes opening.
第一产程到宫口全开为止。消退描述变薄缩短，扩张描述开口。

00:00:53.832 --> 00:01:02.832
The second stage extends from complete dilation until the baby is born. Do not define its start simply as the head entering the birth canal.
第二产程从宫口全开到婴儿出生，不能只把头进入产道当起点。

00:01:02.832 --> 00:01:13.536
The third stage ends when the placenta is delivered. Maternal bleeding and physiology require observation throughout, not only after the placenta appears.
第三产程到胎盘娩出结束。全过程都需观察母体血及生理，不能只等胎盘出现后才看。

00:01:13.536 --> 00:01:26.904
Textbook average times provide context but do not predict an individual birth or justify waiting through deterioration. A previous rapid delivery and the current signs can matter more than an average clock.
教材平均时间只提供背景，不预测个体分娩，也不允许在恶化时等。既往急产及当前征象可能比平均时钟重要。

00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:37.512
Measure contraction frequency from the start of one contraction to the start of the next, and describe duration and intensity separately. Ask whether the pattern is changing.
宫缩频率需从一次开始到下次开始测，持续时间及强度另述，并问模式是否改变。

00:01:37.512 --> 00:01:48.696
A mucus discharge with some blood may be show. Heavy bleeding, shock or severe persistent pain should not be relabelled normal labour just because contractions are present.
黏液夹部分血可为见红。不能因有宫缩就把大量血、休克或持续剧痛说成正常产程。

00:01:48.696 --> 00:02:01.872
Record whether membranes have ruptured, when, and whether fluid was clear, bloody or meconium-stained. Fluid appearance is a clue, not a precise clock or definitive fetal diagnosis.
需记破膜与否、何时及液是否清、血或胎粪染。外观是线索，不是精准计时或确定胎儿诊断。

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:13.080
Do not rupture membranes or perform an internal examination to accelerate assessment. Continue the maternal primary survey and ask the questions that affect immediate preparation.
不能为加快评估人为破膜或内诊。需继续母体主要评估，并问影响即时准备的问题。

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:24.120
Ask about an uncontrollable urge to bear down, grunting or a feeling of needing a bowel movement. These may signal descent and a rapidly approaching birth.
应问无法控制用力、呻吟或似需排便感，这些可提示下降及迅速临近出生。

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:35.856
Explain and obtain appropriate permission for necessary external observation with privacy. A presenting part visible between contractions is a stronger sign than contraction timing alone.
必要外观观察需解释、适当同意及隐私。宫缩间仍见先露，比单凭间隔是更强征象。

00:02:35.856 --> 00:02:46.872
Prepare without trying to hold the baby back or insist on walking to a vehicle. The safest location depends on imminent delivery, resources and the immediate environment.
需准备，不能试图把婴儿挡回或坚持走去车。最安全地点取决于临产程度、资源及即时环境。

00:02:46.872 --> 00:02:57.048
Do not confuse a leg, arm, cord or buttocks with a normal head-first presentation. Recognizing what is actually visible changes the pathway.
不能把腿、臂、脐带或臀误当正常头先露。识别真实可见物会改变路径。

00:02:57.048 --> 00:03:07.800
After birth, the placenta separates and the uterus contracts to help compress vessels at the attachment site. Failure of these mechanisms can produce major bleeding.
出生后胎盘分离，子宫收缩帮助压附着处血管。这些机制失效可产生大量出血。

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:16.608
At the same time, the newborn must establish breathing and maintain warmth. Allocate care so both patients remain observed.
同时新生儿必须建立呼吸并保暖。需分配照护，使双方持续被观察。

00:03:16.608 --> 00:03:25.992
Do not pull the cord to speed the placenta or assume a long third stage is safe while bleeding continues. The patient's condition determines urgency.
不能拉脐带加快胎盘，也不能在持续出血时认第三产程长仍安全。紧迫由患者状态决定。

00:03:25.992 --> 00:03:36.864
Arrange indicated conveyance without waiting simply to finish the stage on scene. Communicate whether the placenta has delivered and what bleeding and perfusion have done.
需安排所需转运，不能只为现场完成产程而等，并交接胎盘是否已出及出血灌注变化。

00:03:36.864 --> 00:03:48.384
Ask about previous births and whether any were rapid. Previous experience can help the patient recognize that birth is close, but it does not eliminate the need for assessment.
需问既往分娩及是否急产。经验可帮助本人认临近出生，但不取消评估需要。

00:03:48.384 --> 00:03:59.400
Use current signs and relevant external observation, not a single contraction interval as proof of inevitable timing. Do not attempt internal dilation measurement.
需用当前征象及相关外观观察，不用单一宫缩间隔证明必然时间，也不尝试内测开指。

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:10.728
Consider the whole move: carrying, loading, road conditions and the ability to deliver safely en route. A long extraction may make immediate preparation necessary.
需考虑全程搬运、装载、路况及途中安全分娩能力。长脱困可使即时准备必要。

00:04:10.728 --> 00:04:21.552
Request help early and explain the plan. A prepared scene can still change rapidly if malpresentation, maternal instability or newborn compromise develops.
需及早求助并解释计划。即使已备现场，异常先露、母不稳或婴受损仍可迅速改局面。

00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:32.808
When birth is not imminent, arrange appropriate conveyance while monitoring progression and maternal status. Avoid promises that birth cannot occur before arrival.
不临近出生时，需安排适当运输，同时监测进展母体，不能保证到院前绝不会生。

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:42.648
When birth is imminent, prepare a safe supported delivery and newborn area. Do not create a dangerous transfer merely to avoid attending a birth.
临近时需备安全支持分娩及新生儿区域，不能只为避免接生而进行危险转移。

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:55.848
A complication can require urgent specialized care while immediate permitted maneuvers occur. Follow the applicable branch and coordinate resources rather than use one transport rule for every presentation.
并发可需急专业照护，同时做获准即时手法。需依相应分支协调资源，不能所有先露同一运输规则。

00:04:55.848 --> 00:05:07.536
If birth becomes imminent during conveyance, coordinate a safe stop when feasible. Effective care and safe vehicle operation matter more than continuing movement at all costs.
途中变临近时，应尽可能协调安全停车。有效照护与车辆安全，比不惜代价继续行驶重要。

00:05:07.536 --> 00:05:18.864
Allocate responsibilities before birth and request additional trained help when needed. A two-person crew may face competing tasks that cannot all be performed safely at once.
出生前需分职责，必要时增训练人员。两人车组可能面对无法同时安全完成的竞争任务。

00:05:18.864 --> 00:05:30.000
One provider must continue maternal observation while newborn support begins. A loud cry attracts attention, but it does not show that the mother is perfusing well.
婴儿支持开始时，仍需一人继续母体观察。大声哭会吸引注意，却不表示母体灌注良好。

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:40.824
Assign communication and timing, including birth time, cord actions and changes in either patient. Use closed-loop requests for equipment and escalation.
需分沟通及计时，包括出生、脐带处理及任一方变化，并以闭环请求器械与升级。

00:05:40.824 --> 00:05:53.520
The diagram is a team-planning aid, not a replacement delivery algorithm. If one patient deteriorates, explicitly redistribute roles instead of silently leaving the other unobserved.
图是团队计划辅助，不替分娩算法。一方恶化时需明确重新分工，不能默默把另一方留作无人观察。

00:05:53.520 --> 00:06:05.952
Use appropriate infection precautions and splash protection. Open and handle the actual birth kit according to its packaging and training rather than assume every kit contains the same supplies.
需适当感染及飞溅防护，并依真实包装训练开用产包，不能假定每包物品相同。

00:06:05.952 --> 00:06:18.744
Prepare dry towels, covering, cord equipment and pads while preserving as much cleanliness and privacy as feasible. A controlled birth takes priority over perfect draping when time is short.
需备干巾、覆盖、脐带器械及垫，尽可能洁净私密。时间紧时受控分娩优先于完美铺巾。

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:32.184
Check suitable newborn mask and ventilation equipment, suction, warmth and assessment tools before they are needed. Merely finding a bag does not prove its valves, mask fit or oxygen configuration work.
需提前查适合婴儿面罩通气、吸引、保温及评估工具。只找到囊，不证明阀、贴合或供氧配置有效。

00:06:32.184 --> 00:06:43.128
Identify missing skills or equipment and request help early. Do not perform an invasive intervention outside role simply because a device happens to be present.
需识别缺技能器械并及早求助。不能因现场刚好有器械就做越权侵入操作。

00:06:43.128 --> 00:06:55.368
Explain the proposed position and ask the patient what helps. A supported lateral, semi-reclined or other appropriate position may be useful according to the situation and trained approach.
需解释拟用体位并问什么有帮助。依情境及训练方法，可用支撑侧卧、半躺或其他合适体位。

00:06:55.368 --> 00:07:05.160
Use a stable surface and adequate limb support. Do not force hip movement through pain or choose a position only because it is convenient for the assistant.
需稳定表面及充分肢体支持。不能强迫疼痛髋活动，也不能只因助手方便选体位。

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:15.912
Maintain access for controlled support and newborn care while avoiding unnecessary exposure. Reassess breathing and perfusion after a major position change.
应保受控支持及婴儿照护接近，同时避多余暴露；大体位变后需复评呼吸灌注。

00:07:15.912 --> 00:07:26.976
Alternative positions are not guarantees against tearing or aspiration. Water-birth physiology claims in the old text are not taught here as permission or a safety assurance.
替代体位不保证无裂伤或误吸。旧教材水中分娩生理说法，这里不当权限或安全保证教。

00:07:26.976 --> 00:07:36.384
Use the trained controlled-support technique as the head emerges. Communicate calmly with the patient rather than shout competing pushing instructions.
头出时需用训练过的受控支持技术，并平静沟通，不能多人喊相互冲突用力指令。

00:07:36.384 --> 00:07:46.992
Support the head and allow its normal turning. The task is not an extraction: do not forcibly pull, twist the neck or hold the presenting part back.
需支持头并容其自然转向。这不是强行脱困，不能强拉、扭颈或把先露挡回。

00:07:46.992 --> 00:07:58.368
If membranes cover an already delivered face, clear them appropriately through the trained birth approach. Do not confuse this with deliberately rupturing membranes before delivery.
已娩脸被膜盖时需依训练方法适当清除，不能与出生前人为破膜混同。

00:07:58.368 --> 00:08:08.400
A slide cannot show the safe amount or direction of hand support. Demonstrate the maneuver on a simulator with the instructor before claiming practical competence.
幻灯不能显示安全手力或方向。需在模拟器及教师指导下演示，再谈实操能力。

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:17.808
Check for a nuchal cord using the trained gentle method after the head is delivered. A loose loop may be reduced without pulling hard on the cord.
头出后应依训练轻柔检查绕颈。松环可适当松解，但不能强拉脐带。

00:08:17.808 --> 00:08:32.280
If the cord is tight and cannot be reduced, use the current complication pathway and seek help. Local pages differ in how they describe the cutting condition, so do not turn every loop into an automatic clamp-and-cut step.
紧且不可松时需现行并发路径及协助。当地页面对剪切条件描述有异，不能每个绕环都自动夹剪。

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:45.024
If clamping and cutting is required under the applicable trained pathway, birth must be completed promptly and newborn support must be ready. Do not cut casually while the body remains trapped.
适用训练路径确需夹剪时，要迅速完成出生并备婴支持，不能身体仍卡时随便剪。

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:54.504
Preserve maternal and newborn observation throughout. Recognition of another complication, such as shoulder dystocia, changes the urgent plan.
全过程仍需观察母婴。识别肩难产等其他并发，会改变急计划。

00:08:54.504 --> 00:09:05.880
As the shoulders deliver, use the trained gentle guidance and support. Do not interpret the textbook directional descriptions as permission to pull strongly on the neck.
肩娩出时需用训练过的轻导支持，不能把教材方向描述理解成允许强拉颈部。

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:15.648
Be ready to support the slippery body as it follows. Maintain secure support without compressing the chest or leaving the newborn suspended by its head.
身体随后会湿滑，需准备支持，并避免压胸或让婴儿以头悬吊。

00:09:15.648 --> 00:09:26.736
If the shoulders do not follow normally, stop forceful attempts, announce the emergency and use the shoulder-dystocia response. More traction is not a solution.
肩不能正常随出时需停止强力尝试、宣布急症并用肩难产应对；更大拉力不是答案。

00:09:26.736 --> 00:09:34.368
Note the birth time when the baby is completely delivered and begin immediate newborn assessment while maternal care continues.
婴完全娩出时需记出生时间，并在母体照护继续时立即评新生儿。

00:09:34.368 --> 00:09:46.368
Assess tone, breathing and heart rate promptly. An apneic or gasping newborn needs the appropriate immediate pathway, not a wait until a scheduled score is calculated.
需迅速评张力、呼吸及心率。无呼吸或喘息婴儿需适当即时路径，不能等到预定评分算完。

00:09:46.368 --> 00:09:57.360
For a well newborn, provide appropriate observed skin-to-skin care and thermal protection. Keep the face visible and the airway supported while continuing evaluation.
状态良好时可适当观察下皮肤接触及保温，并保脸可见、气道有支持及持续评估。

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:08.448
Routine suction is not needed simply because delivery occurred or fluid is meconium-stained. Actual obstruction and the current newborn guideline determine airway clearing.
不能因出生或羊水胎粪染就常规吸引。真实阻塞及现行新生儿指导决定清理。

00:10:08.448 --> 00:10:19.824
The next lecture teaches effective ventilation and the school first-minute drill in detail. Meanwhile, do not let newborn care leave the mother without bleeding and perfusion assessment.
下一节将详教有效通气及学校首分钟演练，同时不能因婴儿照护而漏母体血及灌注。

00:10:19.824 --> 00:10:32.352
Healthy vigorous newborns generally receive deferred cord clamping while assessment and warmth continue. Do not require a compulsory position at the vaginal level to make skin-to-skin care possible.
健康有活力婴儿通常可延迟结扎，同时评估保暖；不需强制与阴道同水平才允许皮肤接触。

00:10:32.352 --> 00:10:45.744
Current local pages are not identical: L zero two describes at least two minutes for vigorous infants, while M zero nine says at least sixty seconds. Keep the page and situation explicit.
现行当地页并不相同：L02描述有活力儿至少两分钟，M09写至少六十秒。需明确页面及情境。

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:58.992
Agree on the current operational plan with the trained team and instructor. Do not postpone necessary effective ventilation merely to satisfy a cord timer or import unreviewed cord-milking techniques.
需与训练团队及教师一致确认当前操作计划。不能为脐带计时延误必要有效通气，也不引入未审挤脐方法。

00:10:58.992 --> 00:11:11.232
When cutting is performed, use the actual trained clamp placement, cut between secure clamps and check for bleeding. Continue assessment rather than assume a completed cut ends cord risk.
夹剪时需依真实训练位置、在可靠夹间剪，并查出血。之后仍需评，不能认剪完就无脐风险。

00:11:11.232 --> 00:11:22.776
Continue maternal observation as the placenta separates. Timing varies, and ongoing bleeding or instability is more important than waiting for the end of a quoted normal interval.
胎盘分离时仍需观察母体。时间有差异，持续血或不稳比等所谓正常区间结束重要。

00:11:22.776 --> 00:11:33.696
Do not pull on the cord, reach in for retained tissue or attempt active placental delivery outside role. These actions can cause serious harm including inversion.
不能拉脐带、伸入取残组织或越权主动娩胎盘，可造成内翻等严重伤害。

00:11:33.696 --> 00:11:43.560
If the placenta delivers, preserve it appropriately for hospital assessment and describe obvious findings without claiming complete exclusion of retained tissue.
娩出后需适当保留供院内检查，并描述明显发现，不能保证彻底排组织残留。

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:53.736
Do not delay indicated conveyance solely to wait for delivery of the placenta. Hand over whether it has delivered, the bleeding trend and maternal response.
不能只为等胎盘而延误所需运输。需交接已出与否、血趋势及母体反应。

00:11:53.736 --> 00:12:05.256
Repeat the maternal primary assessment, visible bleeding and relevant symptoms. Do not let the attention given to a newborn conceal ongoing hemorrhage or neurological illness.
需重复母体主要评估、可见血及症状，不能因关注婴儿而遮持续出血或神经病。

00:12:05.256 --> 00:12:15.792
Continue newborn observation even when the first cry is strong. Temperature, breathing and response can change during wrapping, transfer or transport.
即使首次哭强，仍需婴儿观察。包裹、转移或运输时体温呼吸反应可变。

00:12:15.792 --> 00:12:26.184
Support bonding and appropriate feeding when both are clinically suitable, but never use breastfeeding as a substitute for required resuscitation or hemorrhage control.
双方临床适合时可支持亲子接触及适当喂养，但不能让哺乳替代必要复苏或控血。

00:12:26.184 --> 00:12:35.472
Keep separate records and handover information for each patient. A shared scene does not mean one set of observations can stand for both.
每位需独立记录及交接。同现场不代表一组观察可代双方。

00:12:35.472 --> 00:12:45.432
Name what you actually see and when it occurred. A head already delivered with shoulders failing to follow is different from a presenting limb before the body is born.
需说真实所见及发生时间。头已出而肩不随，与身体前单肢先露不同。

00:12:45.432 --> 00:12:57.048
Declare the complication clearly, ask for the appropriate help and assign continued maternal and newborn responsibilities. Do not let a mnemonic hide an uncertain presentation.
需清楚宣布并发、求适当帮助，并分持续母婴职责。不能让记忆法掩盖不确定先露。

00:12:57.048 --> 00:13:08.856
Use only the permitted trained steps for that emergency while coordinating time-sensitive conveyance. Some specialist maneuvers listed in textbooks are not authorized for the ambulance role.
需在协调时间敏感运输时，只用该急症获准训练步骤。教材某些专业手法不属于救护角色权限。

00:13:08.856 --> 00:13:18.480
Continue reassessment and note the response to each step. Neither a fixed time limit nor a named maneuver guarantees successful delivery.
每步需继续复评及记反应。固定上限或具名手法，都不保证成功分娩。

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:29.424
The school emphasizes shoulder dystocia when the shoulder becomes impacted and birth fails to progress after the head delivers. Retraction of the head can be a clue.
学校强调头出后肩嵌住、出生不进展的肩难产，头回缩可为线索。

00:13:29.424 --> 00:13:40.896
Call for help immediately and track time. Previous dystocia or a larger fetus may increase concern, but absence of those clues does not exclude the emergency.
需立即求助并计时。既往难产或大胎可增担忧，但缺这些也不能排急症。

00:13:40.896 --> 00:13:51.792
Prepare for newborn compromise after birth while continuing maternal support. The immediate objective is a coordinated permitted response, not progressively stronger pulling.
需预备出生后婴受损，同时支持母体。即时目标是协调获准应对，不是逐渐更用力拉。

00:13:51.792 --> 00:14:01.080
Do not press on the uterine fundus or apply forceful head and neck traction. Those are not substitutes for the supervised maneuvers taught next.
不能压宫底或强牵头颈，这些不替代接下来需监督学的手法。

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:11.472
Explain the emergency briefly and coordinate assistance. McRoberts changes the maternal pelvic relationship through hip flexion; it does not pull the baby out.
需简述急症并协调协助。McRoberts通过屈髋改变母体骨盆关系，不是把婴儿拉出。

00:14:11.472 --> 00:14:21.600
Support the legs and bring the thighs toward the abdomen using the trained method. Respect injury, pain and the practical support needed on the actual surface.
需支撑腿，并依训练方法把大腿向腹部屈，考虑伤、痛及真实表面支撑。

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:32.784
Use the maneuver with the appropriate coordinated birth response and reassess progression. Avoid twisting unsupported limbs or assuming more force is always more effective.
需配合适当协调助产应对并复查进展，避免扭无支撑腿，或认更大力总更有效。

00:14:32.784 --> 00:14:43.656
Practise on a simulator with an instructor who can assess hand position, support and coordination. Verbal recall alone cannot establish a safe practical performance.
需在模拟器上由教师评手位、支撑及协调，口头记忆不能独立证明安全实操。

00:14:43.656 --> 00:14:55.536
The school pairs McRoberts with suprapubic pressure to help release an impacted shoulder. Suprapubic identifies the area above the pubic bone, not the upper uterine fundus.
学校把McRoberts与耻骨上压配合松嵌肩。耻骨上是耻骨上方，不是子宫上部宫底。

00:14:55.536 --> 00:15:07.656
Direction, hand placement and timing must follow the actual supervised technique. This lecture distinguishes the concept but does not claim a safe direction can be learned from a label alone.
方向、手位及时间需依真实监督技术。本课区分概念，但不声称只凭标签即可学会安全方向。

00:15:07.656 --> 00:15:15.456
Do not substitute downward fundal pressure. Do not increase head or neck traction because the first attempt did not progress.
不能改用向下宫底压，也不能因首次不进展就加大头颈牵拉。

00:15:15.456 --> 00:15:26.088
Reassess the result and coordinate the next permitted step or escalation. Make the response visible to the team rather than repeat an ineffective maneuver indefinitely.
需复查结果并协调下一获准步或升级，让全队知道反应，不能无限重复无效手法。

00:15:26.088 --> 00:15:36.024
L zero eight explicitly labels several HELPERR steps not authorized. Knowing the whole mnemonic is not permission to perform every action in it.
L08明确把HELPERR若干步标为未授权。知道整套记忆法，不代表可执行每项。

00:15:36.024 --> 00:15:49.032
The prohibited entries include episiotomy, internal rotational maneuvers and removal of the posterior arm. Do not import them from a midwifery or physician description into PCP practice.
未授权项含会阴切开、内部旋转及取后臂，不能把助产士或医生描述搬入PCP实操。

00:15:49.032 --> 00:15:59.760
Hands-and-knees repositioning may be part of the local trained response when feasible. It still needs support, communication and attention to the actual maternal situation.
可行时手膝位可能属当地训练应对，仍需支撑、沟通并关注真实母体情境。

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:12.336
Local escalation timing is an upper planning boundary, not an instruction to wait until it expires. Seek help early, assess response and coordinate urgent movement without unsafe delay.
当地升级时间是计划上界，不是要求等其耗尽。需及早求助、评反应并协调急移动，不能危险延误。

00:16:12.336 --> 00:16:25.176
Breech presentation means buttocks or feet lead rather than the head. Hospital and expert support are preferred when feasible, but the actual stage may make birth on scene unavoidable.
臀位为臀或足先而非头先。可行时优先医院专家，但真实阶段可能使现场出生无法避免。

00:16:25.176 --> 00:16:36.576
If birth is already progressing, follow the trained local support sequence and do not pull on the body or neck. Avoid converting an ankle-lift illustration into uncontrolled traction.
若已在娩出，需依训练当地支持顺序，不能拉躯体或颈，也不能把提踝图变成失控牵拉。

00:16:36.576 --> 00:16:45.672
A delayed head is an immediate emergency requiring resources and urgent planning, not a reason to wait for a quoted threshold before acting.
头延迟是需资源及急计划的即时急症，不能等所引阈值才动。

00:16:45.672 --> 00:16:57.264
Textbook internal-finger and named obstetric rescue techniques are not independent PCP permissions. Protect both patients and coordinate the appropriate assistance and conveyance.
教材内指及具名产科救援技术，不是PCP独立权限。需护双方并协调适当协助运输。

00:16:57.264 --> 00:17:09.720
A visible single limb can indicate a serious abnormal presentation. Describe exactly what is seen and avoid assuming it is an uncomplicated footling breech without the broader context.
可见单肢可能提示严重异常先露。需准确描述，不能无整体背景就认是不复杂足先露臀位。

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:19.104
Support the mother, protect exposed tissue and keep warm through the appropriate pathway. Do not manipulate the limb to test whether it will move.
需依适当路径支持母体、护暴露组织并保暖，不能操弄肢体试它会不会动。

00:17:19.104 --> 00:17:28.392
Do not push the part back or attempt extraction. Arrange urgent conveyance and notification to a facility able to manage the complication.
不能塞回或尝试拉出。需急运并预警有能力处理该并发的机构。

00:17:28.392 --> 00:17:39.912
Continue maternal primary assessment and communicate the presentation and timing. A rare presentation still requires reliable basic care while specialist help is arranged.
需继续母体主要评估，并交接先露及时间。罕见先露也需在安排专家时维持可靠基本照护。

00:17:39.912 --> 00:17:50.664
A cord ahead of the baby may become compressed against the presenting part and pelvis. Declare the emergency and organize immediate appropriate help and conveyance.
脐带在婴前可被先露及骨盆压，需宣布急症并立即安排适当帮助运输。

00:17:50.664 --> 00:17:59.328
Minimize handling and protect the exposed cord according to the current pathway. Do not push it back, repeatedly palpate it or pull on it.
需少触并按现行路径护暴露脐带，不能塞回、反复摸或拉。

00:17:59.328 --> 00:18:12.624
Use the permitted positioning and oxygen instructions while maintaining maternal care. A stationary knee-chest position is not a safe restrained transport position; the movement plan must change appropriately.
需用获准体位给氧并保母体照护。静止膝胸位不是安全运输固定体位，移动计划需适当改变。

00:18:12.624 --> 00:18:25.944
Current L zero eight marks internal elevation of the fetal head not authorized, despite its description in the textbook. Do not adopt that invasive maneuver without actual authorization and training.
现行L08把内抬胎头标为未授权，虽然教材有描述。不能无真实授权训练就采用该侵入手法。

00:18:25.944 --> 00:18:37.752
Meconium-stained fluid should be documented and increases concern for respiratory difficulty. It does not tell you an exact time of fetal compromise or prove aspiration has occurred.
胎粪染液需记，并增呼吸困难担忧。但不告诉准确胎儿受损时间，也不证明已误吸。

00:18:37.752 --> 00:18:48.336
Assess breathing, tone and heart rate immediately. Prepare appropriate airway support rather than repeatedly suction a newborn who needs effective ventilation.
需立即评呼吸张力心率，并备适当气道支持，不能反复吸一个需要有效通气的婴儿。

00:18:48.336 --> 00:19:02.376
The supplied text includes old aggressive and tracheal-suction descriptions. Routine suction simply for meconium, including routine tracheal suction in a nonvigorous infant, is not the current teaching sequence.
自备教材含旧激进及气管吸引描述。仅因胎粪就常规吸，包括无活力儿常规气管吸，不是当前教学顺序。

00:19:02.376 --> 00:19:14.328
Clear genuine obstruction with the appropriate authorized method and reassess effect. The newborn session will distinguish the remaining local-page wording from current obstruction-led guidance.
真实阻塞需以适当授权方法清并复查效果。新生儿节将区分当地页剩余措辞与当前按阻塞决定的指导。

00:19:14.328 --> 00:19:26.280
Preterm describes gestation below thirty-seven weeks; low birth weight describes measured mass. They often overlap but neither can be inferred precisely from appearance alone.
早产描述孕期不足三十七周，低出生体重描述实测质量，两者常重叠但都不能仅凭外观准确推断。

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:38.136
Request appropriate neonatal help and prepare thermal and respiratory support. Do not apply an old oxygen-tent recipe or blanket drying instruction to every gestational age.
需求适当新生儿帮助并备温呼吸支持，不能所有孕期都用旧氧帐配方或一律擦干指令。

00:19:38.136 --> 00:19:53.424
Multiple gestation means additional patients, equipment and possible complications. Label each newborn, record separate birth times and continue separate assessment; smaller size does not guarantee an easier breech birth.
多胎代表更多患者器械及可能并发。需逐婴识别、独立出生时间与评估；小不保证臀位易生。

00:19:53.424 --> 00:20:03.600
Do not let care of a second infant leave the mother unobserved. Recheck bleeding, uterine context and perfusion while resources are redistributed.
不能照护第二婴时留母体无人观察。重分资源时仍需查血、子宫背景及灌注。

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:12.528
Uterine contraction normally compresses vessels where the placenta separated. Atony leaves that mechanical bleeding control inadequate.
正常子宫收缩会压胎盘分离处血管，乏力会使机械止血不足。

00:20:12.528 --> 00:20:20.664
Birth-related tears can bleed even when the fundus is firm. Do not assume every postpartum hemorrhage has a soft uterus.
产伤裂口即使宫底硬仍可出血，不能认每个产后大血都子宫软。

00:20:20.664 --> 00:20:32.328
Retained tissue can interfere with effective contraction, while clotting dysfunction can worsen bleeding. The Four Ts are a search framework, not proof of the exact cause in the field.
残组织可妨有效收缩，凝血异常可恶化血。四T是搜索框架，不证明现场准确病因。

00:20:32.328 --> 00:20:42.792
Consider more than one cause at once and treat current physiology. Recognizing a plausible cause must not delay hemorrhage support and definitive care.
需可同时考虑多因并处理当前生理，找到可能因不能延误出血支持及明确照护。

00:20:42.792 --> 00:20:54.648
The traditional five-hundred-milliliter definition is a reference, not a safe allowance. Ongoing blood loss with hypovolemia requires urgent concern even before that amount is measured.
传统五百毫升定义是参考，不是安全额度。持续失血伴低容量，即使未量到这个数也需急担忧。

00:20:54.648 --> 00:21:06.000
Observe and collect loss when feasible and record the trend. Do not invent exact milliliters from a quick look or ignore blood retained in material or concealed internally.
可行时应观察收集并记趋势，不能扫一眼编准确毫升，也不能漏材料内或内部隐血。

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:16.752
Repeat perfusion, responsiveness and reliable vital signs. A normal initial pressure or a firm fundus does not independently exclude serious hemorrhage.
需复查灌注、反应及可靠生命体征。首次压正常或宫底硬，都不能独立排严重血。

00:21:16.752 --> 00:21:26.664
Declare the concern, mobilize resources and communicate early. Do not finish a perfect paperwork estimate before starting indicated care.
需宣布担忧、调资源并预警，不能先完成完美纸面估计才开始所需照护。

00:21:26.664 --> 00:21:39.072
Assess fundal tone and record whether the placenta has delivered. A firm uterus and an atonic uterus suggest different searches, while neither finding completes the whole assessment.
需评宫底张力并记胎盘已出与否。硬与乏力提示不同搜索，但任何一项都不完成全评。

00:21:39.072 --> 00:21:48.696
Routine massage before placental delivery should not be used to force separation. L zero two describes massage after delivery of the placenta.
不能用胎盘前常规按摩强迫分离，L02描述胎盘出后按摩。

00:21:48.696 --> 00:22:02.880
L zero nine separately allows considering massage when actual postpartum hemorrhage occurs before placental delivery. This is a condition-specific exception, not a reason to massage every undelivered placenta.
L09另允许在胎盘未出但真实产后出血时考虑按摩。这是病情特定例外，不是每个胎盘未出都按摩。

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:13.176
Use the actual trained technique and consultation plan. Do not add cord traction, internal tissue removal or a replacement attempt for suspected inversion.
需用真实训练技术及会诊计划，不能加拉脐带、内部取组织或疑内翻复位尝试。

00:22:13.176 --> 00:22:25.416
Provide indicated airway and oxygen support, maintain warmth and reassess perfusion. The newborn may need a separate provider while maternal resuscitation becomes the immediate priority.
需提供所需气道氧支持、保暖及复查灌注。母体复苏成为即时优先时，婴儿可能需另一人员。

00:22:25.416 --> 00:22:37.848
Manage accessible external laceration bleeding with the appropriate trained direct-pressure method. Do not perform an internal examination or packing simply because a general text mentions it.
可及外裂伤血需适当训练直接压，不能因一般文字提到就内诊或填塞。

00:22:37.848 --> 00:22:52.296
Use actual current fluid and tranexamic-acid conditions, with required prior consultation and response checks. Do not copy wide-open fluid or an old oxytocin infusion recipe into PCP practice.
需用真实现行液体及TXA条件、规定前会诊及反应检查，不能把全开液或旧催产素输注配方复制到PCP。

00:22:52.296 --> 00:23:06.504
Arrange time-sensitive definitive care and update the receiving team. Breastfeeding or voiding when suitable are not substitutes for urgent treatment, and an unstable patient should not be made to walk to a toilet.
需安排时间敏感明确照护并更新接收方。适合时哺乳排尿不能替急治，不稳者也不应被迫走厕所。

00:23:06.504 --> 00:23:22.320
A suspected inverted uterus may present with abnormal protruding tissue, pain, bleeding and shock. Not every form is externally visible, so do not require a dramatic mass before taking deterioration seriously.
疑子宫内翻可有异常外突组织、痛、血及休克，并非每型都可见，不能等巨大外突才认真待恶化。

00:23:22.320 --> 00:23:34.008
Do not pull on an attached placenta or attempt replacement merely because the supplied textbook describes a maneuver. A specialist description is not independent PCP authorization.
不能因自备教材描述就拉附胎盘或试复位。专业描述不等于PCP独立授权。

00:23:34.008 --> 00:23:45.816
Protect exposed tissue appropriately and support airway, warmth and perfusion while arranging urgent expert care. Avoid further manipulation that could worsen bleeding or injury.
需适当护组织，并在安排急专家时支持气道保温灌注，避免进一步操弄恶化血或伤。

00:23:45.816 --> 00:23:58.176
Communicate the observed tissue, placental attachment if known, bleeding and response. Use suspected language when the field finding cannot establish the diagnosis.
需交接所见组织、已知附着、血及反应。现场不能确定时要用疑似措辞。

00:23:58.176 --> 00:24:11.424
The school names the Midwives Regulation. For current context, the Nurses and Midwives Regulation under the HPOA came into effect on April first, twenty twenty-six; the current selected Part five was checked.
学校点名Midwives Regulation。现行背景是HPOA下Nurses and Midwives Regulation于二〇二六年四月一日生效，已核现行第五部分选定内容。

00:24:11.424 --> 00:24:21.816
It describes midwifery assessment, care and emergency measures for midwifery patients and their newborns and infants, subject to limits and conditions.
其描述对助产患者及新生儿婴儿的助产评估、照护及紧急措施，并受限制条件约束。

00:24:21.816 --> 00:24:32.232
A deviation from the normal course requires consultation with a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner and transfer of responsibility when necessary or appropriate.
偏离正常过程时，需与医生或执业护士会诊，并在必要适当时转移照护责任。

00:24:32.232 --> 00:24:42.576
This current-law bridge is not a complete legal opinion or a substitute for the school exam version. Do not present a twenty twenty-one resource sheet as the entire current law.
这项现行法桥梁不是完整法律意见，也不替学校考试版本，不能把二〇二一年资源页当全部现行法。

00:24:42.576 --> 00:24:54.480
BCCNM describes four controls: legislation, college requirements, place-of-practice policies and individual competence. All must fit the actual task and setting.
BCCNM描述四控制：法规、学院要求、执业场所政策及个人能力，都需符合真实任务场所。

00:24:54.480 --> 00:25:06.696
A midwife may have newborn airway or medicine permissions that differ from a paramedic's. That is not proof that every midwife performs every procedure or that one profession is globally senior.
助产士可能有不同于急救人员的新生儿气道或药物权限，但不证明每位都能做全部，也不代表某职业全面上级。

00:25:06.696 --> 00:25:15.408
Ask what care is underway, who is credentialed and what support is needed. Do not infer individual competence from the job title alone.
需问正在做什么、谁有资质及需什么支持，不能只凭职业名推个人能力。

00:25:15.408 --> 00:25:26.304
Their authority does not transfer to you by being present. You remain responsible for actions within your own scope, service requirements and appropriate consultation.
对方在场不会把权限转给你，自己仍需对本角色权限、服务要求及适当会诊内行动负责。

00:25:26.304 --> 00:25:37.536
At a midwife-attended birth, obtain a concise handover and identify who is caring for each patient. Share the immediate concerns before rearranging ongoing care.
助产士在场分娩时需简交接，并识别谁照护各患者；重排正在照护前先共担忧。

00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:51.576
Current L zero one describes midwives as possible primary maternity providers while maternal resuscitation remains a paramedic responsibility. Agree the actual newborn lead according to competence and resources.
现行L01描述助产士可为主要产科提供者，而母体复苏仍由急救人员负责。需依能力资源明确实际新生儿负责人。

00:25:51.576 --> 00:26:05.688
Communicate medicine names, doses and times already given without assuming your role can repeat every agent. Use closed-loop requests and appropriate consultation when responsibilities or destination are unclear.
需交接已用药名量时间，不能假定自己可重复全部。职责或目的地不清时需闭环请求及适当会诊。

00:26:05.688 --> 00:26:19.056
Keep the patient's consent central. Midwife attendance does not automatically clear nonconveyance; any refusal or choice requires the actual assessment, information and applicable process.
同意仍以本人为中心。助产士在场不自动使不运输合格；拒绝选择需真实评估、信息及适用程序。

00:26:19.056 --> 00:26:30.768
This original rehearsal uses an estimated thirty-eight weeks and three days, one previous birth and an increasing urge to push. It is not the school Wednesday scenario.
原创演练为估三十八周三天、一次既往分娩及用力冲动增加，不是学校周三病例。

00:26:30.768 --> 00:26:42.480
Contractions are reported around three minutes apart, but the head is visible between contractions. The external finding outweighs reassurance from an interval that is not less than two minutes.
报告宫缩约三分钟一阵，但间歇仍见头。不能因间隔未短于两分就放心，外观发现更重要。

00:26:42.480 --> 00:26:54.048
Perform the primary assessment, explain preparation and assign maternal and newborn tasks. Do not force the patient to walk or perform an internal exam to prove dilation.
需主要评估、解释准备并分母婴任务，不能强迫走或内诊证明全开。

00:26:54.048 --> 00:27:03.768
Name the equipment and missing resources before birth. The objective is a calm coordinated sequence with explicit changes if a complication appears.
出生前需点器械及缺资源，目标是平静协调，并在并发出现时明确改序。

00:27:03.768 --> 00:27:15.240
Assume birth completes with gentle trained support and the newborn has good tone and an effective cry. Record the complete-birth time and start separate newborn observation.
假设以轻柔训练支持完成出生，婴张力好且有效哭。需记完整出生时间，并开始独立婴观察。

00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:26.976
Use appropriate observed thermal and skin-to-skin care while following the agreed cord plan. Do not perform routine suction or give every vigorous baby one hundred percent oxygen.
需依一致脐计划做适当观察下保温接触，不能常规吸引或给每个有活力婴100%氧。

00:27:26.976 --> 00:27:37.344
The mother is alert but the placenta has not delivered. Continue bleeding and perfusion assessment rather than have the entire team attend only to the newborn.
母清醒但胎盘未出，仍需血及灌注评，不能全队只看婴。

00:27:37.344 --> 00:27:46.656
Explain the next steps and prepare appropriate conveyance. A successful birth does not finish the third-stage or newborn-transition risks.
需解释下一步并备适当运输。成功出生不结束第三产程或婴过渡风险。

00:27:46.656 --> 00:27:59.472
Now assume the placenta has delivered, bleeding continues briskly and the mother becomes pale and lightheaded. Pulse is one hundred twenty-six and pressure eighty-eight over fifty-four.
现假设胎盘已出、血仍快，母苍白头晕，脉一百二十六、压八十八比五十四。

00:27:59.472 --> 00:28:10.272
Total blood loss is uncertain and the fundus appears poorly contracted. Do not delay recognition of hemorrhage while trying to prove exactly five hundred milliliters.
总失血不确定，宫底似收缩差。不能为证明准确五百毫升延误识别。

00:28:10.272 --> 00:28:23.280
Redistribute tasks so maternal authorized hemorrhage care and newborn observation both continue. Use trained fundal care and actual current fluid and medicine conditions with required consultation.
需重分任务，使授权母体出血照护及婴观察均继续，并依训练宫底照护及真实现行液药条件会诊。

00:28:23.280 --> 00:28:33.360
Pre-alert, reassess response and obtain urgent definitive care. A crying baby or delivered placenta must not hide maternal shock.
需预警、复评反应并急取明确照护，不能因婴哭或胎盘已出遮母休克。

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:43.848
Provide the shared obstetric timeline with reliable sources and uncertainties. Include gestation, presentation, complete birth and placental status.
需以可靠来源及未知给共同产科时间线，含孕周、先露、完整出生及胎盘状态。

00:28:43.848 --> 00:28:55.728
Then state maternal findings and trend, observed or estimated blood loss, tone, interventions and response. Do not replace the illness story with normal delivery.
再说母体发现趋势、可见或估失血、张力、干预及反应，不能用正常分娩代替疾病故事。

00:28:55.728 --> 00:29:06.936
Give the newborn's own breathing, heart rate, temperature, resuscitation and timed Apgar information. A score during support needs the support recorded beside it.
需给婴儿自己的呼吸心率温度、复苏及定时Apgar；支持中的分数需旁记支持。

00:29:06.936 --> 00:29:17.544
Identify clinicians and care already provided, including medicines and times, and remaining needs. Clear transfer responsibility matters for both patients.
需识别临床人员及已给照护含药时间，并报剩需。双方都需清楚转移责任。

00:29:17.544 --> 00:29:27.696
For the normal station, explain each preparation and perform the trained simulated support while keeping separate maternal and newborn observations visible.
正常站需解释每项准备并做训练模拟支持，始终使母婴观察独立可见。

00:29:27.696 --> 00:29:40.608
For dystocia, state the observed problem, time, help request and permitted sequence. Demonstrate the difference between suprapubic and fundal location without applying harmful force.
肩难产站需说所见、时间、求助及获准顺序，并演示耻骨上与宫底区别，不施伤害力。

00:29:40.608 --> 00:29:51.504
For hemorrhage, describe mechanism, maternal findings and what changed after care. Do not claim a numerical blood-loss estimate or successful treatment without evidence.
出血站需述机制、母体发现及照护后变化，不能无据声称失血数或治疗成功。

00:29:51.504 --> 00:30:03.648
Use an original simulated case rather than memorize the school assessed answer. Real practical signoff still belongs to the authorized instructor using the actual equipment and criteria.
需用原创模拟例，而非背学校考核答案。真实实操签核仍由授权教师依真实器械标准完成。

00:30:03.648 --> 00:30:11.424
You should explain the stages and use actual signs to anticipate birth without an internal exam or a rigid average-time rule.
应能解释产程，并用真实征象预判出生，不依内诊或僵化平均时间。

00:30:11.424 --> 00:30:23.376
Rehearse normal support and recognize shoulder dystocia, breech, limb or cord complications early. Know which school mnemonic actions are outside the actual paramedic role.
需演练正常支持，并早认肩难产、臀位、肢或脐并发，知道学校记忆法哪些行为超真实角色。

00:30:23.376 --> 00:30:34.368
Connect postpartum bleeding to physiology and current permitted care while maintaining newborn observation. Do not let the emotional success of birth hide new maternal danger.
需把产后血连生理及现行获准照护，同时维持婴观察，不能让出生喜悦遮新母危。

00:30:34.368 --> 00:30:47.544
Finally, coordinate with midwives and receiving teams and verify both patients' responses. The next lecture develops newborn ventilation, compressions and Apgar documentation in detail.
最后需协调助产士及接收团队，并核双方反应。下一节将详教新生儿通气按压及Apgar记录。
